edits_description = "Only the people on the left were used."
final_image_tex = SubResource("Resource_jg17w")
province = 70
blurb = "Depicts the gate of Shimabara, the walled brothel district of Kyoto, at dawn. A drunken customer is being helped home. A courtesan with her attendants are seen on the right.

Shimabara was the only officially licensed pleasure quarter in Kyōto during the Edo period, removed from the Rokujo Misujimachi in 1640 to a more isolated location on the Tamba Highway, surrounded by fields. The main gate on the east side was marked with a willow tree.

This design appears to be based on an illustration by Takehara Shunchōsai in a geographical dictionary from 1780. For example, the group of figures surrounding a drunken customer appears just inside the gate in Shunchōsai's illustration."
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://6kpsqyb2pk7a"
